WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.995
Multiple projects. Multiple coding agents.
Which instructions belong where? Harness

00:00:03.995 --> 00:00:07.991
Desk brings your setup into one local workspace, so you

00:00:07.991 --> 00:00:11.986
can understand it, improve one thing, and check the result.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.382
Choose a project and a coding agent. Global guidance and

00:00:16.382 --> 00:00:19.426
project instructions appear with their source paths. A clean

00:00:19.426 --> 00:00:22.809
folder outside a project has no project instructions to add.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.130
Explore the hierarchy beside a
familiar file tree. Expand skills

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:32.673
and tool sources in groups. Solid
connections show predicted instruction order.

00:00:32.673 --> 00:00:36.803
Dashed connections show available sources,
without claiming they actually loaded.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.686
Open a source, check its scope,
and edit with syntax highlighting.

00:00:41.686 --> 00:00:45.372
Review the diff before saving. A backup is created first. Or

00:00:45.372 --> 00:00:49.058
prepare a scoped question and choose a coding agent to help.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.617
Capture a fresh baseline, then
repeat the same small task after your

00:00:54.617 --> 00:00:59.235
change. Supported adapters collect the reading
automatically. This simulated example shows twelve

00:00:59.235 --> 00:01:03.852
thousand, then nine thousand input
tokens. Real results depend on your setup.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.917
Input tokens include your first prompt. They are not

00:01:07.917 --> 00:01:11.157
a verified breakdown of every file and tool. Keep conditions

00:01:11.157 --> 00:01:14.074
comparable, check the response,
and use a representative task

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:16.991
to see whether the setup still does the job.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.316
Support levels are visible in the app. Several adapters

00:01:21.316 --> 00:01:25.001
have real Mac validation. Claude and Pi still have live

00:01:25.001 --> 00:01:28.318
verification gaps. Kiro reports
context after the response. Windows

00:01:28.318 --> 00:01:31.634
validation and the public package release are in progress.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.689
Start with one project, one agent,
and one worthwhile improvement. Keep

00:01:36.689 --> 00:01:40.378
your sources local, review what you send to an agent, and

00:01:40.378 --> 00:01:44.067
let the evidence guide your next
change. This is Harness Desk.

